# Claude Code local files (NEVER commit)
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Everything about how we work stays out of the public repo.
#
# One directory, one rule — deliberately a directory and not a file list.
# Listing documents by name fails quietly: a new report lands in the root,
# nobody remembers to add a line, and one `git add -A` publishes the internal
# analysis. A directory cannot be forgotten.
#
#   internal/reportes/   analysis and audit write-ups
#   internal/plan/       workplan, roadmaps
#   internal/pruebas/    manual test protocols
#   internal/archivo/    superseded versions
internal/

# Credentials and environment files. NOTHING here is ever needed to run the
# server — SOCRATA_APP_TOKEN is optional and belongs in the MCP client's own
# config — but `.env` is the first file a contributor creates when a README
# mentions an environment variable, and until now nothing stopped it being
# committed. A token in a public repo is a token that must be revoked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
credentials.json
secrets.*
*.secret

# Local tool directories. `.code-review-graph/` ships its own nested .gitignore,
# and that is not enough on its own: `uv build` does not honour nested ignore
# files, which is exactly how an 852 KB SQLite database carrying absolute paths
# under the maintainer's home directory ended up inside a built sdist. The rule
# that protects the repository belongs at the root, where a build tool and a
# careless `git add -A` both have to pass it.
.code-review-graph/
.aider*
.cursor/
.windsurf/

# Data pulled from the portals while debugging. The server itself writes
# nothing to disk by design — keeping data would make the operator a data
# controller under Colombia's Ley 1581 — but a contributor inspecting a
# malformed response naturally saves it next to the code, and portal extracts
# can carry personal data. These never belong in the repository.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.geojson
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.log
!uv.lock

# Test artifacts
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Dev harness and the data it produces. Kept out of the package and out of the
# public repo: it hammers third-party portals and its outputs are large.
sweep/*.jsonl
sweep/*.log
sweep/out/
